From dffb79c9833b1632035666d711d11b0946b80f2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:23:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cli): /reload-mcp on the gateway reports success when
 only the tool-count read times out [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PR #2549 made the classic CLI's gateway /reload-mcp read its tool count with
the full session.info RPC inside the same try as reload.mcp. session.info runs
the unbudgeted inventory build (50-84 s on a loaded mini, per the
REPLY_INVENTORY_BUDGET_S comment) under the client's 30 s RPC timeout, so a
reload that succeeded could print "MCP reload failed".

Why: the count read and the reload shared one except clause, so a failure of
the informational read was judged as a failure of the reload.

Fix: reload.mcp keeps its own failure path; its message prints as soon as it
answers. A GatewayClientError on the following session.info read now prints
"MCP reloaded — tool count unknown (<error>)" (new locale key
cli.reload_mcp.agent_updated_count_unknown, all 17 catalogs) and leaves the
session state untouched.

Proof:
- tests/hermes_cli/test_gateway_reload_mcp.py::test_reload_mcp_count_read_timeout_is_success_with_unknown_count
  RED on origin/main ("❌ MCP reload failed: Gateway did not answer session.info"),
  GREEN with the fix.
- test_reload_mcp_failure_is_still_reported: a reload.mcp timeout still
  prints "MCP reload failed" and never reads the count.
- 9 affected files (reload/mcp/cli_info/i18n suites): 145 passed.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok.

Follow-up to review t_01a1d66bab4ab82c (GitHub review 5897167317), nit 1.
Card: t_01a1d684d734713a
